  "body": "**Builds on #348 - includes its commits; merge after #348.** (A cross-fork PR can't target the fork branch, so this targets `main`. The #355 change itself is commit a840ce4; once #348 merges, this branch takes `git merge upstream/main` and the diff shrinks to that commit.)\n\n## What changed\n- MCP tools `export_tool_library {path}` and `import_tool_library {path}` (`crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs`), each with a schema that requires one string `path`.\n  - Export writes the document's tools in the same format as the Tool library page's Export (`tool_library::export_tool_library`).\n  - Import checks the file with `parse_tool_library`, then runs #348's undoable `ImportTools` command through the session History, so the import is one undo step. As in the GUI, an identical tool is skipped, a clashing name arrives as \"Name (2)\", and a malformed or insane file is refused naming the tool.\n  - Refusals come back as MCP tool errors: an unreadable file, an unwritable path, a document with no tools to export, or \"nothing to import\".\n- Matching job-script verbs `cam.exportTools(path)` and `cam.importTools(path)` are in the VERBS table and `assets/scripts/cam.d.ts`. The MCP tools call these verbs, so the MCP lane and the batch lane share one meaning per verb (#128).\n- `docs/decisions/355-mcp-tool-library.md`\n\n## Readings\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test mcp`: 8/8 pass.\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-app --test scripting`: 18/18 pass. This includes `the_bindings_file_is_the_verb_table`, which checks that `cam.d.ts` matches VERBS.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (after merging upstream/main):\n  - app suites: all pass;\n  - ui suites: only the known reds that also fail on upstream main:\n    - the GPU headless tests `headless_run_succeeds`, `headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero` and `egui_headless_cli_exit_code_is_zero`;\n    - the `egui_shell_snapshot_light` golden (#255).\n\n## Pinning tests\n- `handshake_and_tool_list` (updated): both tools are listed with a required `path`.\n- `tool_library_export_import_roundtrip_into_a_fresh_document`\n- `tool_library_import_skips_duplicates_and_renames_clashes`\n- `tool_library_malformed_files_are_refused_by_name`\n- `tool_library_import_is_one_undo_step`\n- `script_tool_library_verbs_roundtrip` (scripting)\n\n## Not exercised\n- The `camcraft-cli mcp` stdio binary was not driven by a real MCP client. The tests drive the in-process handler.\n- #348 detects duplicates by name, so re-importing \"B\" into a document that already holds \"B (2)\" yields \"B (3)\". This is recorded in the decisions file; changing it is a call for #348 or a follow-up.\n\nChangelog: MCP `export_tool_library` / `import_tool_library` tools and `cam.exportTools` / `cam.importTools` script verbs (#355)\n\nFixes #355\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
